# The clang-tidy configuration of src/ (issue #8; notes/modernization-plan.md, sections 4.1, 4.2 and
# 8). Run it through tools/tidy.py, never with clang-tidy --fix directly: until M5 no fix may touch
# the arguments of TASSERT*, TERROR* or TEND*, which are stringized into the exception messages that
# error.txt records and difftest compares. tools/tidy.py reports the findings inside those arguments
# apart and reverts every fix inside them.
#
# The checks follow the coding standard of plan section 8: owning raw pointers and new/delete
# (cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory, -no-malloc), C string and formatting functions
# (bugprone-unsafe-functions, cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg, modernize-use-std-print), nullptr,
# override, enum class and [[nodiscard]], using instead of typedef (issue #35), the <c...> forms of the C
# headers (issue #40), and the bug-prone
# patterns. The checks that are noise for a reconstruction (its parameter lists and integer types are
# the original's) are off.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  cppcoreguidelines-no-malloc,
  cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  cppcoreguidelines-use-enum-class,
  modernize-deprecated-headers,
  modernize-use-nodiscard,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-std-print,
  modernize-use-using
WarningsAsErrors: ''
# The headers of src/, not those of src/Extern (third-party code in its own style).
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\\]src[/\\].*'
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\\]Extern[/\\].*'
FormatStyle: file
CheckOptions:
  bugprone-unsafe-functions.ReportMoreUnsafeFunctions: true
  # The C headers that the headers of src/ include (common.h, ContentWindows.h, Talk.h) too, not only the
  # main files' (issue #40).
  modernize-deprecated-headers.CheckHeaderFile: true
